<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Pre-Raid Best in Slot Gear list for Shadow Priest DPS in Cataclysm Classic. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, Bind on Equip drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">Best in Slot Gear for Shadow Priest DPS Pre-Raid</h2>With Reforging added, BiS lists are not set in stone in the same way they once were. Most items can be replaced for similar items of the same item level, and generally a higher item level will be a better item with few exceptions.<br/>
<br/>The primary exceptions here are in regards to Hit and Haste. Equipping a higher item level piece that causes you to lose your Hit Cap is very rarely going to be worth it, but in a lot of cases some smart Reforging can fix this for you. For the first time, Haste is primarily worth it at various breakpoints, and falling between them for a small item level gain could be a DPS loss, but this is the kind of thing you will have to sim to figure out.<br/>
<br/>While there is a variety of different pieces that can be considered Pre-Raid BiS, some of them naturally end up being expensive BoEs,behind luck-based <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/skill=794/archaeology">
<img alt="Archaeology" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_archaeology.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Archaeology</span></a> grinds, or cost several weeks worth of <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a>.<br/>
<br/>Due to this, the gear embed below has both an optimized and a more realistic setup to choose from, though most players will likely end up with something inbetween. <br/>
<br/>As a quick recap, these are the stats we are mainly looking for on our Pre-BiS pieces, as they will be the most impactful when first stepping into a raid:<ol>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Intellect - As a primary and most important stat, we almost always prioritize Intellect on any new gear piece.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Spirit/<wbr/>Hit Rating - You always want to reach your Hit Cap of 17%, and this is done through either Spirit or Hit Rating. If you have to choose between the two, grab Spirit.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Haste Rating - Haste is great, with breakpoints that massively impact our DPS.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Mastery and Crit Chance - These two stats are both nice to have but are more incidental gains rather than something to keep an eye on.</div></li></ol>
<ul></ul>
<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="justice-points">Justice Points for Shadow Priest DPS Pre-Raid</h3>
<a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=395/justice-points">
<span>
<img alt="Justice Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-justice.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Justice Points</span></span></a> are the Cataclysm version of <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=101/emblem-of-heroism">
<span>
<img alt="Emblem of Heroism" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_proclaimchampion.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Heroism</span></span></a>, which means that they can be obtained by killing bosses in Heroic Dungeons and completing Random Dungeons through the Random Dungeon Finder tool. The main vendors you can exchange these at to obtain gear are <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/npc=46555/gunra">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Gunra</span></a> for the Horde and <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/npc=44246/magatha-silverton">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Magatha Silverton</span></a> for the Alliance.<br/>
<br/>The order you purchase items here is heavily dependent on your luck. None of the items available for <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=395/justice-points">
<span>
<img alt="Justice Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-justice.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Justice Points</span></span></a> are the best option in the slot, so grab what you think will be upgraded last. Something like <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=58183/soul-casket">
<img alt="Soul Casket" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_enggizmos_12.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Soul Casket</span></a> can be a good filler if you have had bad luck with that slot, while other items like <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=58188/band-of-secret-names">
<img alt="Band of Secret Names" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_diamondring1.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Band of Secret Names</span></a> pieces are individually strong but are overshadowed by <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> options.<br/>
<br/>
