<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="valor-points">Valor Points for Shadow Priest DPS Pre-Raid</h3>
<a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> are the Cataclysm's version of Raid Emblems, which means that they can be obtained by killing bosses in Raids and completing Heroic Dungeons through the Random Dungeon Finder tool. The main vendors you can exchange these at to obtain gear are <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/npc=46556/jamusvaz">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Jamus'Vaz</span></a> for the Horde and <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/npc=44245/faldren-tillsdale">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Faldren Tillsdale</span></a> for the Alliance.<br/>
<br/> There is a weekly cap of 1000 <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a>, meaning any purchase using this currency will take multiple weeks to complete. With this in mind, it is recommended to prioritize your tier pieces first. This cap carries over week to week, so you won't be falling behind on <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> if you missed the cap for one week. <br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=71279/vestment-of-the-cleansing-flame">
<img alt="Vestment of the Cleansing Flame" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_robe_raidpriest_j_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vestment of the Cleansing Flame</span></a> is recommended as your top priority. Both of the other Tier pieces are potential drops in <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=5600/baradin-hold">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Baradin Hold</span></a>, making it better to try your luck there. Depending on your luck with the Tier Head &amp; Shoulders, you might want to save your <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> and buy non-Tier pieces earlier.<br/>
<br/>Outside of that, quite a few of the items listed are your BiS option, especially if you aren't willing to spend massive amounts of gold on BoE <span class="q4">Epics</span>.<br/>
<br/>
